  (Y, "The properties explain choices that look arbitrary otherwise. They explain why a string, a number and a tuple of numbers are acceptable keys while a list is not, why 1 and 1.0 find the same pair, and why an object that can change must not be used to find a pair, since a pair filed under one hash value would be lost when the key changes."),
